# Copy to tests/e2e/.env.e2e (gitignored) to supply the e2e web build with
# a real, test-safe backend instead of running against nothing. Supabase
# anon/publishable keys are public-by-design (protected by RLS), so this is
# not a secret in the credential-leak sense — but this file must still
# never be committed, and must never hold service-role or other privileged
# keys.
#
# Values here follow the same shape scripts/cloudflare-build.sh requires
# (read-only reference, not modified by this harness).
#
# KAN-166 note (2026-09-09): no real test-safe anon key was available at
# harness-build time. SUPABASE_URL is the real, public project endpoint —
# not a secret — with an obviously-fake, self-describing placeholder for
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. tests/e2e/support/fixtures.ts classifies the
# resulting 401 by name (Supabase-URL response, status 401) as a known,
# non-fatal signal rather than letting it fail the run or hiding it
# silently. Replace the placeholder with a real test-safe key when one is
# available — see the KAN-166 Jira comment / agent/status/devops.md.

SUPABASE_URL=https://wtncuzcskpigqpmnxwws.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=test-placeholder-not-a-real-key
APP_NAME=Dabbler
ENVIRONMENT=test
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
